<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia Seal says to buy, develop land.</title>
<headline>Malaysia Seal says to buy, develop land.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian timber products firm Seal Inc Bhd said on Tuesday its directors have agreed to buy a 32.4 acre land for 22.6 million ringgit.</p>
<p>It plans to develop the land into an industrial property with expected development cost of 45 million ringgit, and sale revenue of 77 million ringgit, Seal said in a statement.</p>
<p>It expects to reap total pretax profit of 32 million ringgit from the sale of units in the proposed development, located in central Selangor state.</p>
<p>Seal said the project would help the company diversify into industrial property development.</p>
<p>It also asked for the requotation of its stock from Wednesday. Seal shares were suspended from May 12, being last traded at 4.86 ringgit.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
